# This is the action definition for the Fibonacci action.
# The goal is to compute the Fibonacci sequence up to the 'order' specified in the goal.
# The result will contain the Fibonacci sequence as a list of integers.     
# The feedback will contain the current Fibonacci sequence being computed.
# The action definition consists of three parts: Goal, Result, and Feedback.
# The Goal part defines the input to the action, which is the 'order' of the Fibonacci sequence to compute.
# The Result part defines the output of the action, which is the computed Fibonacci sequence.
# The Feedback part defines the intermediate feedback that can be sent during the execution of the action,
# which is the current Fibonacci sequence being computed at that point in time.

int32 order
---
int32[] sequence
---
int32[] current_sequence